the top leaders of china's ruling  communist party are holding a key  meeting that's expected to further  tighten president xi jinping's grip on  power behind closed doors she is set to  lay the groundwork for an unprecedented  third term in office that would cement  his position as china's most powerful  leader in recent history  chinese president xi jinping hasn't left  china for over 21 months partly because  of covet 19 but also because he's  focused on building his power base at  home  the upcoming plenum is an opportunity to  set the tone in his bid to become  china's long-term ruler his message is  that china is a superpower and the rest  of the world better know it  the chinese people will never allow any  foreign forces to bully oppress or  enslave us  anyone who dares try to do that will  have their heads bashed and bloodied  against the great wall of steel forged  by over 1.4 billion chinese people  the plenum gathers 370 top communist  party cadres from politics and the  military the most important item on the  agenda is a resolution looking back at  key events in the party's hundred-year  history it gives the party the ability  to shape the narrative of its history as  it sees fit and enshrined president xi's  role as leader  it's only the third time this has  happened  the previous two resolutions were  introduced by the founder of the  people's republic of china mao zedong  and the architect of the economic  reforms that boosted the economy deng  xiaoping  she wants to show that he's an equally  important leader transforming china into  a global power  he wants to make his power felt across  all of chinese society  he has boosted the military and launched  a crackdown that has muzzle tech tycoons  like alibaba's jack ma  in recent weeks she has been stepping up  pressure on the sovereign island of  taiwan which china considers its own and  the world is watching to see how  tensions unfold  the plenum which runs until thursday  lays the groundwork for the crucial 2022  party congress where she is expected to  secure his position for at least another  five years  he faces challenges economic growth is  slowing down amid an energy crunch  supply chain disruption and fears of a  crisis in the country's real estate  sector  challenges that need to be overcome if  he is to prove himself equal to chairman  mao and don xiaoping  and let's bring in fabian kretschmer  in beijing for us um fabian this morning  the communist party central committee  gathered behind closed doors as we just  heard i know we're not in there but what  can we expect from the meeting  well i mean it might sound like a rather  bureaucratic meeting but indeed it's  crucial  for seating ping to lay the groundwork  of his  power extended he wants to stay in power  for a third term that's unprecedented  and what we can expect is that the  members of the central committee they  will adopt a so-called historic  resolution to praise the historic  achievements of the communist party in  the last 100 years since its founding  what that means is basically a rewriting  of history  forexing pink uh to use for its own  agenda  and um it's quite remarkable that uh  those um historical resolutions have  only been passed uh three times one time  uh under mao zedong that was in 1945 and  he used a chance to sideline his  opponents with that resolution later  under deng xiaoping he used a historic  resolution to reflect on history and  also reflect on the party's mistakes but  now we basically have a historic  resolution to rewrite history uh to lay  the groundwork for xi jinping's power to  um yeah keep on going  and what did today's events then mean  for president xi jinping this resolution  and so on how does that help him  well i mean it's quite a sensitive issue  here um no chinese leader has ever  stayed in power for a third office since  mao zedong and um after mao's death um  the party  decided that  there should not be any excessive power  there should not be any excessive  personality cult and um xi jinping is  basically the first politician to change  that he's the most powerful leader since  mao zedong and  basically the propaganda narrative here  so the message is that he's the leader  to lead the chinese nation um to become  great again and become strength uh  strong again and there's no alternative  to him  and how much do the 1.3 billion members  of the chinese nation actually get to  know about this meeting  well it's highly controlled first of all  the meeting is taking place behind  closed doors i mean not even we  journalists have any access there will  be a news handout in the coming days and  but what the public  notices uh first of all is an increase  of personality cult in the recent weeks  and months the state media have  exaggerated their praise of xi jinping  it became almost absurd i mean it's  comparable to the rhetoric of  the north korean regime almost and um  also what i find remarkable is that if  you talk to people on the street  especially in the countryside most of  them are not really aware that xi  jinping is the first  leader who will change the law to become  a de facto leader for life and  i think right now is a really a  sensitive time and you can really feel  that the authorities are quite nervous  and yeah  so um exciting times to watch out what's  happening in the next days and thank you  so much for following them for us fabian  kretschmer reporting live from beijing  you
 

